# frontier-harness
# `fh onboard` writes the approved repository capability manifest to <repo>/.harness/.
# It is per-worktree runtime state bound to an approval recorded in the state root, not
# something a checkout should carry: a committed policy would arrive in every clone with no
# approval behind it. Until now this was only excluded per-clone via .git/info/exclude, so a
# fresh clone offered it for commit.
.harness/
